<H3>1.4&nbsp;&nbsp; Grading, Hilbert series and degree bound</H3><!--SEC END -->
Powerful properties of an invariant ring are its grading and the
associated Hilbert series. As a <I>K</I>-vector space, <I>I</I>(<I>G</I>) is not
finite dimensional. However, since the action of <I>G</I> preserves the
degree of polynomials, <I>I</I>(<I>G</I>) decomposes into the direct sum of its
homogeneous components:
