through a Gröbner basis computation with CoCoA&nbsp;[<A HREF="#CoCoA"><CITE>4</CITE></A>], using
theorem&nbsp;2.7.9 of&nbsp;[<A HREF="#Sturmfels.AIT"><CITE>29</CITE></A>]. However, our set was not
minimal since we had not removed the invariant <B><I>x</I></B><SUP><FONT SIZE=2><B><I>c</I></B></FONT></SUP><SUP><FONT SIZE=2>&circ;*</FONT></SUP> where <B><I>c</I></B> is
the complete graph. The set above can now be computed in about one
second with Kemper's implementation of <TT>Invar</TT>  in
