positive integer coefficient, then there exists a system of parameters
of degrees (<I>d</I><SUB><FONT SIZE=2>1</FONT></SUB>,...,<I>d</I><SUB><FONT SIZE=2><I>m</I></FONT></SUB>). A counter-example has been found, but
the conjecture still holds if the representation of <I>G</I> over <I>V</I> is
irreducible, or when using a multigraded Hilbert series (one grading
for each irreducible component)&nbsp;[<A HREF="#Dixmier.1991"><CITE>7</CITE></A><CITE>, p.&nbsp;5</CITE>].<BR>
